          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Acute, nonprogressive, asymmetric, and",
              "pdf_page": 612,
              "printed_page": 530,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Restrict until diagnosis is made in case of nonpainful spinal cord disease—presence of vertebral column instability from other causes these characteristics greatly helps in diagnosis such as intervertebral disc herniation or of fibrocartilaginous embolic myelopathy fracture/luxation. (FCE).",
              "pdf_page": 612,
              "printed_page": 530,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Once FCE is confirmed, activity should be encouraged, not restricted.",
              "pdf_page": 612,
              "printed_page": 530,
              "column": 2
